        {
            "id": "93c3e79b-c4b9-40e9-bfe6-373d5d9690a5",
            "build_id": "528781fe-3ee1-427d-b2ea-e123d5cfe3ce",
            "round_number": 4,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-08-10T18:11:31.130524+00:00",
            "notes": "[Crusader Hydraulics](item_b64cee07-ca32-405d-987e-868b415bbc09) is the key. This essentially makes you 10% more tanky as long as you have shields or armor (1.1x your HP). It also means that whenever you are healing yourself with [Inner Peace](item_3cb26943-7c02-4aa2-97d0-7411dac1073c) and you're healing shields or armor, it is 10% more valuable. If you are going against a lot of AP enemies, then you can do the same by just getting [Reinforced Titanium](item_8ebaa7db-aedf-48ed-adc1-318cb46a3214) (or both).\n\nFor our damage item we take [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) in most rounds. I also often take [Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f) because 25 armor is nice and the attack speed helps a lot VS shields. [Orb of Perception](item_762bf2a4-c062-4dfd-b8e0-47e37ba1cadf) is another good alternative. If you have a lot of money, then taking [Eye of the Spider](item_bbaf01d7-340d-4199-b738-86a98d68fe9b) is great too. You can also do [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) with a rare item of your choice if you have a lot of cash, I really like [Transference Protocol](item_04d5d433-9493-4094-b4e6-77d632a236e9) as well.\n\n### COUNTERPICK OPTIONS - INSTEAD OF THE 1-2 GREEN HP ITEMS OR IF ENOUGH MONEY, CONSIDER GETTING THESE IN THE ROUNDS GOING FORWARD\n\n[Iron Eyes](item_f16d03a7-f20e-4a1d-a1f6-55863e163c03) vs. heroes that like to headshot like Kiri, Cass, Soldier, Genji (melee is crit if they play the item), Ashe (AD), Ana (crit Power), JQ (AD), or Zen. The more I play, the more I value it because Zen is so easy to headshot.\n\n[Cushioned Padding](item_20f2f4bc-4611-4d1f-b653-20f04d56b96f) vs. DoT (Damage over Time) and debuffs such as Ashe, Ana, JQ, Mei, Moira, and Junkrat (burn Power). There are some other debuffs and slows where it\u2019s still useful, mostly from items or powers.",
